{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run","id":995565,"title":"[2E] Grimoires and Relics - How to run?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T02:55:31-07:00","id":995565,"title":"[2E] Grimoires and Relics - How to run?","content":"Tomes of immerse power. Manuals on the roads to Legacies. Temptations to become Left Handed? Secrets of deepest Mysteries? Topic about how to utilize Grimoires and other 'magical items', Relics in short ( yes, Artifacts, Imbued Items, Fetishes and many other 'magical' thing ).<br /> <br /> There is cool one plot in <b>Agents of SHIELD</b> this year about <i>Darkhold</i>, that is Marvels 'Book of Sins'. Best clip on it is in <a href=\"http://abc.go.com/shows/marvels-agents-of-shield/video/most-recent/VDKA3472919\" target=\"_blank\">that link</a> - sadly people outside US will have problem viewing it. To cheer up, it's in S04E05 'Lockup' episode.<br /> <br /> In above clip there is cool idea that book is blank, but the showing letters on physical contact with it, in readers first language. How can effect like that replicated? Some Mind+Matter spell?<br /> <br /> I also can share mine spells ideas that let you 'clone' in perfect condition any book you have - adding Prime 1 to it, you can replicate Rotes also in it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Copying (Matter \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> By means of this spell, the mage can copy the item he is seeing with materials that are suitable to it\u2019s composition. Many Mysterium apprentices makes copies of precious books from just stashes of ink and paper by this spell.<br /> When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, the original items return to their original form.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the spell\u2019s Duration is Lasting.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>For copying complex mechanisms.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022:</b> Mage can copy also any Rote found in the original Grimoire, like with \u2018Scribe Grimoire\u2019 Prime \u2022 spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Printing (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> Like in \u2018Copying\u2019 spell, only any solid material will be good for copy. Reach and Prime option are the same.<br /> <br /> <b>Duplicate (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Pattering<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> To witness, item just come in two exactly the same things, like cell is dividing itself. Reach and Prime option are the same like in \u2018Copying\u2019 spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-30-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:55:46-07:00","id":995610,"title":"","content":"There's a book kind of like that already in one of the books,I think it's Night Horrors, whichever book the False Awakening is in. That might give you some ideas.<br /> <br /> Why do Printing and Duplicate do exactly the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:15:58-07:00","id":995642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run?p=995610#post995610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Printing and Duplicate do exactly the same thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>All 3 spells make the same things - they copy books. Printing and Duplicate are different that first need any solid matter ( for examples stones ), second just makes books like 'mitosis of cells' but made on book itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-30-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:22:59-07:00","id":995646,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. Okay, you may want to change the wording for the last spell because what it actually does isn't getting across at all, it just looks like you're drawing a weird distinction between solid matter and gases for no reason. I'd delete the first two sentences of the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:46:28-07:00","id":995654,"title":"","content":"Why not just make Printing and Duplicate part of Copying, but use part of Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:42:39-07:00","id":995681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run?p=995654#post995654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just make Printing and Duplicate part of Copying, but use part of Reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it would make them possible to lower dots mages. You do not want Apprentices to copy each Grimoire by sacrificing 1-3 hours and risking Paradox in Atheneum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:39:05-07:00","id":995721,"title":"","content":"Ostensibly, you don't want apprentice Mastigoi using mind control spells on your Sleepwalker librarians to make them identify potentially dangerous books but at the end of the day, they <i>can</i> do it. The Awakened can do what they do because they can do it; the risks and consequences are things their society can, does, and should plan for.<br /> <br /> Also, grimoires <i>aren't</i> just simple books. You need magic involved. Copying a grimoire is essentially the same spell as creating a grimoire. In other words, all these spells need Prime at an equivalent level because you're doing the same thing with Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:23:29-07:00","id":995739,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and Scribe Grimoire is available at Prime 1. And all one needs is a notebook or tablet or chalkboard. I appreciate that the Matter lets you do that without them, but then you're working on longer spells that could require Indefinite duration. Most mages should be able to find something to write on or with without requiring magic. Worse comes to worst you could just scribe it onto your shirt or smartphone until you get to something more permanent.<br /> <br /> I plan on implementing them the way I do most troves of knowledge. Part treasure, part trap, often a pathway to corruption. For instance there's a ghost that's a daimonomikon with a few hidden rotes in him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-30-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:30:26-07:00","id":995858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run?p=995681#post995681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it would make them possible to lower dots mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see no problems for starting level mages to do all this. Hells, I could see it done as a training exercise. All that you need to do is contain the paradox, or use mana, and no problem. At least with my games; if its an issue with your games, I just don't see it. Sorry, I just see more benefit plus more potential plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-30-2016, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:42:25-07:00","id":995881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run?p=995858#post995858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see no problems for starting level mages to do all this. Hells, I could see it done as a training exercise. All that you need to do is contain the paradox, or use mana, and no problem. At least with my games; if its an issue with your games, I just don't see it. Sorry, I just see more benefit plus more potential plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that it would break the scaling of the Matter Arcanum. Turning one substance into something unrelated requires at least Matter 4 (Transubstantiation). The Patterning practice is needed for it to be possible, and lower-rated practices should not be able to do so.<br /> <br /> For gameplay reasons it becomes incredibly unbalanced since that principle would allow a Matter 2 mage to create a spell that does this with everything. And if you get it as a Rote you've gained huge parts of both Matter 3 and Matter 4 for a single XP (instead of 8 XP and possibly Gnosis requirements).<br /> And if you don't allow it with other stuff than books, why would you be able to do it with books in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-30-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:54:25-07:00","id":995885,"title":"","content":"You have to be able to cast it with Improvised Spellcasting. If you don't have the dots in the Arcana you couldn't cast it from a grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:18:53-07:00","id":995896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995565-2e-grimoires-and-relics-how-to-run?p=995885#post995885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to be able to cast it with Improvised Spellcasting. If you don't have the dots in the Arcana you couldn't cast it from a grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misremembered the spells. I thought they were about grimoires and not just books in general with grimoires as an option. I'll edit my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-30-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T01:10:38-07:00","id":995996,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> says - I'm totally okay with Apprentices at Matter 2 locked in the 'copy room' of Atheneum, with stashes of paper and ink. Also logical be that one of Mysterium Matter Adepts is making for the proper 'Copiest' of Order, creating perfect copies of books and Grimoires ( with Prime 1 ) out of nothing. Apprentice that makes copies of tomes out of nothing seems bad idea as implications on Matter Arcanum would be too much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:32:16-07:00","id":997125,"title":"","content":"The Primary Factor for this spell should be &quot;Duration&quot; not Potency (the spell doesn't even seem to use Potency), since a &quot;more powerful version of the spell&quot; would be one that lasted longer before the ink just started running down the pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}